# Frozen pre-regeneration baseline (Stage 2a). Byte-identical copies of the
# eight files in data/INPUTS.sha256, kept so nothing in Stage 2a can destroy
# the only record of what the current manuscript draft reports. Verify with
# `cd data/baseline_frozen && shasum -a 256 -c INPUTS.sha256`.
data/baseline_frozen/

# Large data files — regenerate by running Notebook 1
# (comment out these lines if you want to track them in git)
data/processed/DATA_all.json

# Synthetic corpora. Each is ~200 MB and regenerable on demand from the seed,
# configuration and commit recorded in its own runmeta.json:
#     cd src && python corpus.py <label>
# The PROVENANCE is tracked and the data are not: runmeta.json, the validity
# rejections and the pLCA groupings are small and stay in git, and
# data/INPUTS.sha256 pins the checksums of the large files so any copy can be
# proven genuine.
data/processed/corpus_*/values.parquet
data/processed/corpus_*/metrics.parquet
data/processed/corpus_*/parents.json.gz

# Nested git repo (cloned GitHub copy — not needed here)
CompareUQMethods/

# Void/scratch notebooks
notebooks/VOID_*
notebooks/_SCRATCHPAD.ipynb
notebooks/CompareUQMethods_backup.ipynb

# Reference PDFs and third-party datasets (copyrighted publisher files,
# large supplementary data). Kept locally for consultation, never committed
# to this public repository.
refs/

# Manuscript drafts. Kept local: the working .docx carries unresolved comments
# from named third parties, and this repository is public and Zenodo-archived.
# Remove this rule only for a clean copy with comments resolved and accepted.
outputs/manuscript/
